Write Python source only. Function candidate_starts(scan,query,minimum_identity,max_start). Return sorted unique integer candidate start offsets 0<=s<max_start. This is exhaustive for ungapped full-length Hamming matching, not heuristic: allowed=floor(len(query)*(1-minimum_identity)+1e-9); partition query into allowed+1 nonempty consecutive blocks covering entire query. Any match with at most allowed mismatches has one exact block by pigeonhole principle. For each block offset a and text query[a:b], use repeated scan.find(block, search_from), each found index p implies candidate p-a. Keep if in bounds and s+len(query)<=len(scan). If allowed>=len(query), return range all valid starts. Handle empty query ValueError and minimum_identity outside(0,1] ValueError. Partition boundaries a=i*len(query)//blocks,b=(i+1)*len(query)//blocks. Do not score matches, do not reverse complement, no IO. Under40 lines. Include imports math only if used.
